  "result": "**Verdict: `OK`** — first gate run, 5 of 6 runs unused.\n\n**Body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/region_entry.lean`):\n\n```lean\ndef overlaps : Formula := .atom \"rel_occupies\" [aU, aR] []\ndef body : Formula := .rises overlaps\n```\n\nThe two elements are the same atom read under one operator: `rel_occupies u r` for \"comes to overlap a structure region at the observation\", and `rises` for \"did not overlap it at the observation before\". No region quantifier (the record names `r` as a formal), no parameter, no literal, no concept call. `narrowings` is empty — the contract plus the record's justification fix the reading, so there was nothing left to choose.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/region_entry.lean`): one instance with nothing to fill; a shared geometry of a 20 m square junction polygon (region 100) and a car (track 1) heading north at 10 m/s, three scenes a second apart.\n\n- `holds`: y = −15, −5, 5 m — clear then inside; window at t = 1000 → compliant\n- `fails`: y = −5, 0, 5 m — inside throughout; window t = 1000–2000 → violated\n- `blind`: the `holds` geometry with `rel.occupies` masked; window at t = 1000 → unknown for that atom alone\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: each witness sets `window` rather than padding. `rises` looks back one observation, so it is truncated at a trace's first scene, and padding would repeat a scene at which the event is *false* — which would turn `holds` into a violation. The windows name the instants the narratives actually speak about and keep the truncated scene out, so no history `boundary` is declared.\n\n`task_result.md` is written at `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-001/code/concept__drv_motion_region_entry/task_result.md`.",
